--- a/src/follower.c
+++ b/src/follower.c
@@ -0,0 +1,2352 @@
+// The lead Pokemon walks behind the player, as in HeartGold/SoulSilver
+// (PC port only; [Gameplay] FollowingPokemon in the ini turns it off).
+//
+// What could be taken from the HGSS decompilation (pret/pokeheartgold) is
+// ported as it is there:
+//  - The follower is the first Pokemon that can still battle, or the first
+//    that isn't an Egg if none can (FollowMon_InitMapObject).
+//  - It goes back into its Ball while the player rides a Bike or surfs, and
+//    the tallest Pokemon stay out of buildings (MAP_FOLLOWMODE_HEIGHT_RESTRICT,
+//    tp_param.csv's too_tall).
+//  - Its mood: -127..127, reset whenever a different Pokemon starts following,
+//    moved one step towards 0 for every step taken while it's out, and
+//    changed by battles and items (pokemon_mood.c, FieldSystem_UnkSub108_*).
+//    HGSS keeps it in the Pokemon's data; here it's kept in RAM so saves stay
+//    the same as the original game's.
+//  - Its lines when talked to (msg_0265.gmm, see data/follower_messages.h).
+// HGSS picks those lines in native code that isn't decompiled yet, so which
+// line comes up, the emote bubbles, the little animations and the items it
+// finds are a recreation, as is the way it follows (map objects work
+// differently on the DS).
+//
+// The follower is an ordinary object event with a reserved local id and
+// graphics id; it isn't saved (SaveObjectEvents leaves it out) and is set up
+// again after loading. Its graphics are built at run time from the sprite
+// pack (port/follower_pack.c): HGSS-style overworld sprites from
+// pokeemerald-expansion, with their own palette drawn through one of the
+// port's extra sprite palettes.
+
